# Line endings are pinned on purpose.
#
# lib/, components/, hooks/, app/api/ and public/ are byte-for-byte copies of the
# upstream pi-web checkout, and the desktop checks verify that with `diff -r`.
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, which rewrites every LF to
# CRLF in the working tree on checkout — a fresh clone would then differ from
# upstream in every file and the comparison would mean nothing. Normalising to LF
# in the repository and checking out LF everywhere keeps those copies honest.
#
# text=auto still leaves real binaries (icons, fonts) untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
